[StudyName "Mikhail Tal vs. Georgi Tringov"]
[ChapterName "Amsterdam 1964 (2)"]
[UTCDate "2021.05.01"]
[UTCTime "14:32:51"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/BlunderOven"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/SeOsShhE/vy7dR32N"]

1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 c6 {Black makes an unnecessary pawn move,
before he has finished developing. Stronger was} (4... Nf6) 5. Bg5 {The other
active bishop move, 5.♗c4, was not so effective, since there the bishop could
become an object of attack by a later ...b7-b5 or ...d6-d5.} (5. Bc4 {[%csl
Gd5,Gb5][%cal Gd6d5,Gb7b5]}) 5... Qb6? {And this is already a serious mistake.
It was essential to play 5...♘f6.} (5... Nf6) 6. Qd2! {Instead of passively
defending the pawn, White prepares its sacrifice and gains additional tempi for
development.} 6... Qxb2 7. Rb1 Qa3 8. Bc4 Qa5 9. O-O e6 10. Rfe1 a6 11. Bf4 e5
(11... Qc7) 12. dxe5 dxe5 13. Qd6! Qxc3 14. Red1 Nd7 15. Bxf7+ Kxf7 16. Ng5+ Ke8
17. Qe6+ {1-0 Black resigns.} 1-0

